=== Climate ===
Noto Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate (Köppen climate classification ''Am''), moderated by the warm Shendan currents that flow around the peninsula. The climate is characterised by hot, humid conditions year-round with a distinct wet season from May through October, when the Shendan monsoon brings torrential rainfall and occasional typhoon landfalls. The peninsula's position projecting into the open Shendan makes it particularly exposed to typhoon impacts, and the prefecture has experienced several devastating storms in its modern history.

The mountainous interior creates significant microclimatic variation. The windward eastern coast receives heavier rainfall and stronger winds, while the leeward western coast is relatively sheltered and supports the peninsula's agricultural operations. The central valleys experience frequent fog, which the lacquerware artisans historically valued for its role in the slow-curing process of urushi lacquer.

